10708	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s4","entry":{"id":"review-6cda40b87e5f3fa9333d3b900925ab01","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:05:27.108Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed exclusions satisfy upstream s4 ac1.","evidence":"DEF §6.4 ac1 requires: 'Given an operation that git supports ... the operation is reachable through a named tool for its family'. The LLD explicitly excludes bisect, interactive operations, mail and server commands. Neither that criterion nor the HLD grants these exclusions. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Obtain an upstream scope amendment or design named tools for the excluded supported operations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The registry currently registers the stated 22 git tools, and shared git failure helpers lack typed failures.","evidence":"Read registerGitTools in full: it registers all 22 listed definitions. helpers.ts spawnFail returns output, format, success and error; fail returns the same fields without failure. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Preserve these ids and existing rendered failure fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing shared contracts provide output checking, typed calls and fail-safe approval resolution.","evidence":"callTool requires TypedTool with typebox inputSchema and outputSchema. executeTool validates input, checks successful data against outputSchema and returns schema-mismatch on missing or invalid data. resolveApprovalClass catches a throwing predicate and returns 'destructive'; shouldAsk always asks for that class. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Consume these implementations without duplicating their pipeline stages; preserve concrete schema types on exported tool definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Changing shared spawnFail and fail covers existing git failures with the new typed-failure invariant.","evidence":"branch.ts defines its own local spawnFail and fail. status.ts constructs failed results inline. merge.ts returns a conflict result with 'success: false, error: merge conflict, data' without calling fail. executeTool returns unsuccessful tool results immediately: 'if (!result.success) return result', so it does not fill in missing failure kinds. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/branch.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/status.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/merge.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Inventory and update local helpers, inline failures and conflict branches across all 22 tools, preserving their individual output text and data.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The timeout helper change specifies the caller changes needed to detect timeouts.","evidence":"push.ts calls 'fail(git_push, result.stderr, result.stdout, result.code)' without timedOut; worktree.ts uses the same four-argument pattern. runShell exposes timedOut separately from code and signal. Merely adding optional opts to fail leaves those calls unable to distinguish a timeout from another killed command. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/worktree.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Specify updating every relevant failure call to pass ShellResult.timedOut and truncation metadata, including conflict-detection paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Existing input schemas can remain JSON-identical while rejecting dash-prefixed and NUL-containing arguments through schema patterns.","evidence":"push.ts defines remote and ref as unrestricted 'type: string'; branch.ts likewise defines name and startPoint without patterns. approval-class-mapping.test.ts compares serialized live input schemas with the original snapshot using deepEqual. Adding the promised rejection patterns changes those schemas; preserving them leaves the promised schema rejection absent. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/branch.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/fixtures/approval-snapshot.json]","action":"Resolve the compatibility policy explicitly. Either approve schema tightening or retain schemas and specify runtime argument validation and safe argv construction, with regression tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Timeout failures can add an unknown-outcome warning while preserving every existing output and error string exactly.","evidence":"helpers.ts computes msg from stderr, stdout or exit code, then returns 'output: [id] failed: msg' and 'error: msg'. It adds no unknown-outcome warning. The LLD simultaneously requires that warning for mutation timeouts and exact preservation of these fields. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts]","action":"Put the new warning in failure.message while preserving legacy fields, or explicitly document the permitted rendered-message change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Production caller migration remains owned by s7, while s4 owns git schemas, parsing and destructive classification.","evidence":"HLD §5.4 assigns git families, schemas, destructive operations and porcelain parsing to s4. §5.7 assigns rewriting direct spawn sites and removing wrappers to s7. The LLD's migration step 8 explicitly leaves production call-site migration to s7. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Treat the production files listed under new-tool call sites as future consumers, not edits in this Story.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared shell result supports reliable detection of spawn errors, timeouts and truncated stdout.","evidence":"Read the complete runShell implementation: the error event sets spawnError; the timeout callback sets timedOut before SIGKILL; stdout byte accounting sets stdoutTruncated when stdoutBytes exceeds maxBytes. These values are returned on completion. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Use these flags before parsing or classifying git failures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The fail helper has enough information to add mutation-specific timeout guidance.","evidence":"The proposed signature accepts id, process text, code and timeout/truncation flags, but no operation or mutation indicator. Existing branch and worktree ids multiplex reads and mutations. The LLD does not specify an id/operation classification mechanism or where callers add the mutation-specific warning. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/branch.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/worktree.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Define a mutation-aware failure context or assign warning construction explicitly to the tool call sites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed coverage-table test proves upstream ac1's complete operation coverage.","evidence":"Upstream DEF ac1 quantifies over supported git operations. The LLD's coverage test only compares registered ids with a self-authored table and checks that covered and excluded operations do not overlap. A family absent from both lists passes these checks, and an excluded supported operation remains unreachable. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Define an independently reviewed operation inventory and assert each required operation has an executable, tested tool/input mapping; resolve exclusions against upstream ac1.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing snapshot provides a reusable regression check for original ids and serialized input schemas.","evidence":"Read the full mapping test: its final test iterates the baseline snapshot, asserts each original id remains registered, and deep-compares JSON-serialized inputSchema with the stored schema. Its comment explicitly allows later Stories to add tools outside that baseline. [files: src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/fixtures/approval-snapshot.json]","action":"Keep the original 228-entry baseline immutable; record new tools separately and update approval expectations without replacing historical schema evidence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":5,"med":1,"low":6,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T15:05:27.108Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
