8692	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s4","entry":{"id":"review-eb4f307029f6f59b902585fee74887d7","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:11:11.037Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The coverage table's exclusions and mappings satisfy upstream s4 ac1.","evidence":"DEF s4 ac1 requires: 'Given an operation that git supports ... the operation is reachable through a named tool for its family'. The design instead permits plumbing exclusions because a command 'has no caller', and maps write-tree and commit-tree to git_commit. The actual git_commit input has message, author, signing and commit guards; its execute body invokes git commit and cannot expose write-tree or commit-tree semantics. Recording a mapping does not make those operations reachable. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/commit.ts]","action":"Specify executable inputs for each covered operation and obtain an upstream scope decision for exclusions before treating ac1 as met.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current registry contains 22 git tools, and shared git failure helpers return legacy text without typed failure.","evidence":"registerGitTools registers 22 definitions. helpers.ts spawnFail returns output '[id] cannot spawn git -- ...', error 'git not found'; fail chooses stderr.trim() || stdout.trim() || `exit ${code}`. Neither sets failure. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Preserve these legacy fields when adding typed failures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_show currently ignores a failed numstat read and succeeds with an empty file list.","evidence":"show.ts uses 'const files = stat.code === 0 ? parseNumstat(stat.stdout) : []' and subsequently returns success: true with data. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts]","action":"Keep the documented compatibility behavior and add the proposed warning.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing shared contracts support TypeBox output schemas, typed calls, and input-dependent approval with destructive fallback on exceptions.","evidence":"Tool.outputSchema is TSchema; TypedTool requires TypeBox inputSchema and outputSchema; callTool derives input and result through Static. resolveApprovalClass catches approval-function exceptions and returns 'destructive'. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Consume these existing contracts without redefining them; retain schema inference in exported tool definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed family surface covers the existing range-base reader's git operations without changing existing tool inputs.","evidence":"range-base.ts introducingCommit invokes git log '--diff-filter=A', '--format=%H', '-1', '--', relPath. git_log's complete schema offers cwd, ref, path, limit, author, grep, since and until, with additionalProperties:false; the design preserves that schema and supplies no new log operation exposing diff-filter. Its new tools therefore cannot reproduce this caller's provenance query. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/log.ts]","action":"Add a named typed operation supporting the introducing-commit query, while preserving the old git_log schema, and include it in the s7 handoff inventory.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Keeping JSON-identical input schemas is sufficient to preserve existing accepted calls after adding outputSchema.","evidence":"executor.ts starts input validation only when outputSchema is declared. git_log currently accepts any numeric limit and clampLimit floors and clamps it, while its advertised schema specifies minimum:1 and maximum:500. Adding outputSchema activates validation, so inputs previously normalized by execute, such as limit:0 or 501, fail before execution despite identical schema JSON. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/log.ts]","action":"Explicitly resolve runtime input compatibility for newly validated legacy tools; test previously normalized inputs, rather than only schema snapshots.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Deferring production call-site migration to s7 respects the upstream ownership split.","evidence":"HLD §5.4 assigns git family schemas, destructive classification and porcelain parsing to s4. §5.7 assigns the direct-spawn inventory, repository check, caller rewrite and old-wrapper removal to s7. The design's migration step 8 leaves that rewrite to s7. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Keep the listed production consumers as handoff requirements, rather than editing their execution paths in s4.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ShellResult supplies the timeout and truncation signals required by the proposed failure handling.","evidence":"runShell sets timedOut before SIGKILL, returns code and signal on close, and reports stdoutTruncated when stdoutBytes > maxBytes. These fields exist on ShellResult. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/merge.ts]","action":"Check timeout before conflict classification and truncation before parsing, including secondary reads.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed secondary-read handling makes git_show command failures visible.","evidence":"show.ts runs both diffArgv and statArgv, but only stat.code influences files; diff.code, diff.spawnError and diff.timedOut are never checked before success:true. The design explicitly adds warnings for numstat, yet does not specify handling for the equally ignored diff failure. Passing flags to fail cannot help a path that never calls fail; the registration wrapper also only catches unsuccessful results. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Define and test handling for failed or truncated diff reads and inventory other ignored helper reads, with an explicit compatibility decision for each.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed coverage tests prove upstream ac1 operation reachability.","evidence":"Upstream ac1 requires an operation to be 'reachable through a named tool'. The planned coverage tests check command membership and registered tool ids. Existing git_commit demonstrates the gap: its schema has no tree or parent inputs and executes git commit, yet the design would count write-tree and commit-tree as covered by that id. Those tests can pass with inaccessible operations. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/commit.ts]","action":"Add operation-level cases that invoke the mapped tool with concrete inputs and verify each operation's semantics; test exclusions against approved upstream scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":5,"med":0,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T15:11:11.037Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
