8459	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s4","entry":{"id":"review-c503213da68fa18a68ae4ff7cd9cd32e","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:26:25.462Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The coverage table maps covered commands to tools with inputs capable of reaching those operations.","evidence":"DEF s4 ac1 requires an operation to be 'reachable through a named tool'. The design maps config to git_config, but declares only git_config_get and git_config_set. It maps var and version to git_rev_parse, whose declared inputs expose neither operation. Recording executable coverage cases cannot resolve these missing dispatch contracts. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/index.ts]","action":"Reconcile every coverage row with a declared tool and concrete operation-selecting input before claiming complete coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"git_fetch mutations currently have common approval and will stay common.","evidence":"fetch.ts explicitly says 'no approval required by default', and gitFetchTool has no approval property. resolveApprovalClass returns 'none' when approval is undefined. Changing fetch to common adds approval in manual and edit-auto modes; it is not preservation of today's class. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Describe fetch's approval change explicitly and reconcile it with the stated read and compatibility invariants.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_show currently ignores failure of its main diff read while treating a failed numstat read as an empty file list.","evidence":"After awaiting diff and stat, execute computes 'const files = stat.code === 0 ? parseNumstat(stat.stdout) : []' and returns success true without checking diff.code or diff.spawnError. The proposed distinction addresses actual existing behavior. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts]","action":"Implement the specified main-read failure and auxiliary-read warning distinction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing shared executor supports output validation, typed calls, destructive approval and the proposed approval test seam.","evidence":"Tool declares outputSchema and ApprovalClass; callTool takes a TypedTool definition and derives Static input/output types. executeTool validates input and successful data, always asks for destructive calls, and exports _setApprovalGateForTests. These capabilities can be consumed without introducing another pipeline. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Reuse these existing contracts and preserve concrete schema types on exported tool definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"git_path_history supplies the introducing-commit query required by both range-base.ts and anchor-finder.ts.","evidence":"range-base.ts queries HEAD history for a SHA, but findAnchor queries an explicit trackingRef using '--format=%H%x09%cI'. parseAnchorLog requires both SHA and time, returning UNKNOWN if either is absent. The proposed tool has no revision/trackingRef input and returns only '{commits: {sha}[]}', so it cannot preserve the anchor query's branch or timestamp semantics. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/team/anchor-finder.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Add an explicit revision input and committer timestamp output, and hand off tests covering a tracking branch different from HEAD and preservation of firstCommitTime.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Keeping git_show's input schema JSON-identical lets the existing executor reject maxBytes 100 against its schema.","evidence":"show.ts declares maxBytes with only 'type: number' and a description; its minimum of 1024 exists solely in Math.max inside execute. Unlike diff.ts, its schema has no minimum or maximum. executeTool rejects only values that fail validateAgainstSchema. A JSON-identical replacement therefore accepts 100 and execute still clamps it, contradicting the required rejection test. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Choose explicitly between preserving this schema and adding bounds; if rejection is required, document the schema compatibility exception and update the baseline intentionally.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Git-specific schemas, parsing and approval classification belong to s4, while executor mechanics and production caller migration remain owned by other stories.","evidence":"HLD §5 assigns git families and destructive classification to s4, schema checking to s2, approval exchange to s3, and direct-spawn migration to s7. The design's implementation steps add git-family behavior and explicitly defer production call-site movement to s7, matching those boundaries. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Keep caller migration deferred while supplying complete contracts for its consumers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Spawn failures, timeouts and truncated stdout can be detected from the existing shell runner without redesigning its result contract.","evidence":"ShellResult exposes spawnError, timedOut and stdoutTruncated. runShell sets timedOut before SIGKILL, records spawn errors, and computes stdoutTruncated from captured byte counts. The proposed helpers and parser guards can consume these existing signals. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/merge.ts]","action":"Propagate these flags at every call site, including auxiliary and conflict-detection reads.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s4 acceptance criterion has a corresponding planned test category.","evidence":"DEF s4 defines ac1 reachability, ac2 checked results, ac3 destructive classification and ac4 existing ids/meaning. The design maps these respectively to executable coverage cases, schema/parser/failure tests, approval tests through executeTool, and legacy surface/output compatibility tests. The existing snapshot test already compares serialized input schemas for every baseline id. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Retain this mapping, correcting the incompatible schema and incomplete history contract identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T15:26:25.462Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
