8488	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s4","entry":{"id":"review-52574314d843b7397f94d6f1c2c99057","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:04:00.989Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The long tail of git operations belongs to s8, while s4 retains existing tools and the reads needed by s7.","evidence":"S008/EXT.md explicitly states: 'Story s4 keeps the 22 existing tools and the read tools s7 needs.' DEF §6.8 assigns remaining unattended commands and stdin delivery to s8. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S008/EXT.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Preserve this split.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_show currently ignores failures of its main diff read and tolerates a failed numstat read.","evidence":"execute awaits diff and stat, sets 'const files = stat.code === 0 ? parseNumstat(stat.stdout) : []', and returns success without checking diff.code or diff.spawnError. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts]","action":"Implement the explicitly accepted main-read failure change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"depth values below 1 already fail in git, so enabling input validation introduces no additional depth compatibility change.","evidence":"fetch.ts computes depth with Math.floor and then uses 'if (depth) { argv.push(`--depth=${depth}`); }'. depth: 0 is omitted and an ordinary fetch runs, although its inputSchema declares minimum: 1. The executor will reject it once outputSchema is declared. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Include depth: 0 and fractional values flooring to zero in the compatibility audit, decision and tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The checked-result executor and typed call helper already provide the shared mechanisms this Story consumes.","evidence":"callTool requires a TypedTool with typebox inputSchema and outputSchema and delegates to executeTool. executeTool validates inputs when outputSchema exists, validates successful data and returns schema-mismatch for invalid data. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Reuse these implementations without adding a parallel validation pipeline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"git_merge_base supports all common ancestors with the proposed result shape {base?: string, isAncestor?: boolean}.","evidence":"The installed git 2.53.0 help states '--all output all common ancestors'. The proposed output exposes only one base string, so multiple merge bases cannot be represented as individual checked values. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Define a bases array for all:true and specify the no-common-ancestor result and exit-code handling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new path-history contract includes the information required by the two named history callers.","evidence":"range-base's introducingCommit invokes log with '--diff-filter=A', '--format=%H', '-1' and a path. findAnchor invokes log with '--first-parent', '--diff-filter=A', '--reverse', '--format=%H%x09%cI', trackingRef and a policy path; parseAnchorLog preserves both SHA and timestamp. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/team/anchor-finder.ts]","action":"Keep the proposed HEAD and divergent tracking-ref comparison tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Legacy merge conflicts carry data and a distinct error string that must survive failure enrichment.","evidence":"merge.ts returns success:false, error:'merge conflict' and GitMergeData containing inConflict:true and conflicts. The executor returns failed tool results directly, without successful-data schema validation. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/merge.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve the complete failed result when attaching failure, as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s4 can consume s3's destructive approval and exception fallback without redesigning approval infrastructure.","evidence":"resolveApprovalClass catches classifier exceptions and returns 'destructive'. shouldAsk immediately returns true for destructive. executeTool obtains approval before calling tool.execute and returns a denied result when approval is absent. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Limit changes to git classifiers and their tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The secondary-read inventory accounts for the reads that otherwise could silently produce incomplete successful mutation results.","evidence":"collectCommitData performs a third read, 'git show --numstat --format= HEAD', besides the two SHA reads. It parses stat.stdout without checking code, spawnError, timedOut or stdoutTruncated. The design names only commit's SHA and short-SHA lookups for warnings, leaving failed or cut statistics without an explicit handling rule despite its checked-output invariant. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/commit.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Inventory this statistics read and define complete parsing, truncation handling and success-with-warning behavior after the commit succeeds. Add corresponding tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShell exposes the signals required to distinguish spawn failures, timeouts and truncated stdout.","evidence":"ShellResult includes spawnError, timedOut and stdoutTruncated. runShell sets timedOut before SIGKILL and computes stdoutTruncated from captured byte counts on both error and close paths. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Use these fields rather than inferring truncation from string length.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The planned coverage test consistently implements the three-owner inventory required by the amended scope.","evidence":"LLD §3.4 explicitly permits 'covered', 'assigned' and 'excluded' and requires assigned rows not to count as covered. Its unit-test strategy instead requires every recorded command to be 'in exactly one of covered or excluded'. DEF §6.8 and S008/EXT.md confirm that remaining commands belong to s8. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S008/EXT.md]","action":"Make the unit-test strategy use all three owners, retaining runnable cases only for covered rows. Keep the existing ac1–ac4 mapping with the error-path and compatibility additions above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":2,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T16:04:00.989Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
