7983	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s4","entry":{"id":"review-fd36f7afa370d44ebb265cc3897ccfde","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:10:04.234Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reduced s4 scope leaves the remaining git commands to s8 while retaining existing tools and reads needed by s7.","evidence":"AMD-8 states: 'Story s4 keeps the 22 existing tools and the read tools s7 needs.' EXT-s8 requires the remaining unattended commands, stdin delivery, destructive classifications and combined coverage. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-8.json, .insrc/artifacts/EXT-b7a68147dcf72034-s8.json]","action":"Keep the explicit distinction between assigned and covered commands.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_show currently ignores the main diff outcome, and commit statistics parse stdout without checking the secondary command outcome.","evidence":"show.ts checks 'stat.code === 0' for files but renders diff.stdout and returns success without checking diff.code. collectCommitData runs three commands and iterates 'stat.stdout.split' without checking its outcome. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/commit.ts]","action":"Implement the specified main-read failure and secondary-read warnings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_fetch depth 0 or 0.5 currently omits --depth, while its input schema requires minimum 1.","evidence":"fetch.ts declares 'minimum: 1', floors depth with Math.floor, and adds the option only under 'if (depth)'. The executor currently checks input only when outputSchema is declared; fetch declares none. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain the explicit compatibility tests for both values.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared checked executor, typed call helper and approval test seam already exist with the shapes consumed here.","evidence":"callTool accepts a definition with typebox inputSchema and outputSchema and returns schema-derived data. executeTool checks input and successful data, then runs hooks. _setApprovalGateForTests is exported; resolveApprovalClass catches exceptions and returns destructive. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Reuse these contracts without changing their ownership.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The ignored-secondary-read inventory accounts for the existing git tool lookups that need failure handling.","evidence":"reset.ts additionally runs 'const afterShort = await runShell' after the reset and renders 'afterShort.stdout.trim()' without checking the outcome. push.ts calls 'const shortSha = await revParse(cwd, ref)' after pushing; helpers.ts turns a failed revParse into ''. Neither lookup is included in the warning inventory, and GitPushData is omitted from the types receiving warnings. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/reset.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Inventory these secondary reads explicitly and specify their preserved placeholders, classification and warnings, including GitPushData if warnings are intended for every secondary lookup.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every existing failure retains its exact output and error text after output schemas enable input validation, apart from the enumerated accepted changes.","evidence":"git_diff currently returns output '[git:diff] invalid-input: `exclude` must be an array of non-empty strings' and error 'invalid-input' for malformed exclude. Its schema already rejects that input. Once outputSchema is present, executeTool returns 'input for tool git_diff does not fit its input schema: ...' before execute runs, changing both fields. The design's compatibility exceptions enumerate numeric bounds but not these existing invalid-input paths. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Document these additional input-validation compatibility changes and adjust the legacy-failure tests, or explicitly design a way to preserve these failures within the shared contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Approval exchange, schema checking and hook execution remain shared-story responsibilities rather than being reimplemented by git tools.","evidence":"The existing executor owns schema validation, broker-backed approval and withHooks. approval-policy.ts owns destructive-always-asks behavior. AMD-8 delegates the remaining git family work to s8; the proposed git changes supply schemas and classifications to these existing stages. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-8.json]","action":"Keep git-specific message classification and parsing inside the git family.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shell contract provides the signals needed to distinguish spawn failure, timeout and truncated structured reads.","evidence":"ShellResult declares spawnError, timedOut and stdoutTruncated. runShell sets timedOut before SIGKILL and computes stdoutTruncated from captured byte counts on both error and close paths. Existing git helpers currently discard these distinctions, matching the proposed need to propagate them. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts]","action":"Pass the complete outcome through every relevant failure path before parsing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping covers s4's four upstream acceptance criteria within the amended scope.","evidence":"DEF s4 defines named operation coverage, checked results, destructive classification and preservation of existing ids/meaning. The design maps these respectively to coverage cases, schema/parser/failure tests, executor approval tests and compatibility snapshots. The existing approval-class-mapping test already compares serialized input schemas against the 228-tool baseline and explicitly permits later tools outside that baseline. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, .insrc/artifacts/EXT-b7a68147dcf72034-s8.json, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Preserve the original 228-tool baseline when adding new-tool coverage, and resolve the compatibility exception identified above before implementing its assertions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T16:10:04.234Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
