9347	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s4","entry":{"id":"review-02badec71f987783033c0af0daee642f","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:39:13.898Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The approved upstream scope permits s4 and s8 together to meet the full git coverage criterion.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md records: \"DEF s4 ac1 ... is met by s4 and s8 together\" and records approval of DEF revision 2 and AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-8. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Keep this explicit qualification in the coverage documentation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"git_for_each_ref with the designed merged and pointsAt inputs covers branch --no-merged.","evidence":"The designed input provides merged but no inverse selector. Installed git 2.53.0's for-each-ref help distinguishes \"--merged <commit> print only refs that are merged\" from \"--no-merged <commit> print only refs that are not merged\". The existing git_branch schema offers only list/create/switch/delete and cannot supply the missing filter either. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/branch.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S004/LLD.md]","action":"Define an explicit negative merged filter and its semantics, or assign --no-merged to s8 instead of claiming coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_show currently ignores failure of its main diff read while allowing a failed numstat read to yield an empty file list.","evidence":"After awaiting diff and stat, execute uses \"stat.code === 0 ? parseNumstat(stat.stdout) : []\" and constructs a successful result without checking diff.code, diff.spawnError or diff.timedOut. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/show.ts]","action":"Implement the stated distinction between main-read failure and secondary-read warning.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"git_fetch depth 0 and 0.5 currently omit --depth rather than failing.","evidence":"execute computes \"Math.floor(input['depth'])\" and adds the option only under \"if (depth)\". Its schema independently declares \"minimum: 1\". [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/fetch.ts]","action":"Retain the documented compatibility change and rejection tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing typed helper and executor support TypeBox schemas, input checking and checked result data as described.","evidence":"call-tool.ts defines \"TypedTool = Tool & { readonly inputSchema: TSchema; readonly outputSchema: TSchema }\" and derives input/result types with Static. executeTool validates input when outputSchema exists, checks successful result.data, and returns schema-mismatch on invalid data. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Preserve concrete schema types on exported tool definitions so callers retain inference.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The claimed complete helper-read inventory assigns handling to every existing lookup.","evidence":"amend.ts's wasPushed performs three additional reads and returns false on failed HEAD/upstream resolution; reset.ts's willNeedForcePush returns \"r.code === 0\"; merge.ts's listConflicts returns [] on a failed read. These helpers and their distinct expected non-zero outcomes are absent from the claimed complete inventory. Merely checking code currently hides timeout, truncation and spawn failures. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/amend.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/reset.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/merge.ts]","action":"Inventory these helpers explicitly. Define missing-upstream/non-ancestor behavior separately from process failure, and specify warning or failure handling for failed conflict enumeration. Add targeted tests instead of leaving these choices to a future grep audit.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An existing snapshot can enforce preservation of legacy tool ids and serialized input schemas.","evidence":"approval-class-mapping.test.ts loads the pre-rewrite snapshot, asserts its length is 228, checks every old id remains registered, and compares JSON-serialized live inputSchema with old.inputSchema using deepEqual. Its comparison deliberately permits new tools. [files: src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/fixtures/approval-snapshot.json]","action":"Keep the original 228-tool baseline immutable; record new tools separately when updating approval expectations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Per-call destructive classification consumes the existing s3 approval contract without requiring a new approval exchange.","evidence":"Tool.approval already accepts ApprovalClass or an input function. resolveApprovalClass catches a throwing function and returns destructive; shouldAsk returns true for destructive before consulting the common mode. executeTool uses the daemon gate and rejects unmatched or declined approvals. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Keep git-specific classification inside the family and reuse the existing executor gate.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed runShellBytes bounds preserve the corpus reader's existing diagnostics-limit behavior.","evidence":"BinaryGitOptions has separate stdoutLimit and stderrLimit. createGitRunner terminates with \"Git diagnostics exceed byte limit\" when stderr exceeds its limit; READER_LIMITS sets stderrBytes to 65536 and allows callers to lower it independently. ShellOptions exposes only maxBytes, and the proposed contract bounds stderr to that shared output limit without stating overflow failure or an independent diagnostics budget. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Add an independent stderr limit and detectable overflow behavior to the byte runner/tool contract, or explicitly preserve that enforcement in the s7 adapter. Test independently lowered diagnostics limits.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed isolation environment and Git read arguments match the existing corpus reader.","evidence":"gitEnvironment constructs a fresh PATH/SystemRoot environment with the listed locale and Git variables. GIT_READ_ARGS contains --no-replace-objects, --literal-pathspecs, protocol.allow=never, and disabled fsmonitor, hooks and attributes files, matching the design. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts]","action":"Move these definitions to the shared module without weakening them.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s4 acceptance criterion has a corresponding planned test category.","evidence":"DEF §6.4 specifies coverage, checked result shapes, destructive classification and legacy identity/meaning. The design maps these respectively to coverage/integration cases, schema/parser/failure cases, approval/executor-denial cases, and snapshot/legacy-result cases. Existing diff tests already demonstrate the proposed node:test, temporary-repository and injected-shell approach. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/__tests__/diff.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Retain these mappings and add cases for the coverage and helper-inventory gaps identified above. This verifies the test plan, not implementation of the proposed tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T17:39:13.898Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
